share your cooking with other people. You don't. Be good for your mother. Okay, Alonzo? Stay safe.

14
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:53,100
I will call his name that he is now. Mr. Northup, I have two gentlemen whose acquaintance you should

15
00:08:53,100 --> 00:09:00,640
make. Mr. Brown and Hamilton. Sir? Mr. Northup, these two gentlemen were inquiring about distinguished

16
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:06,400
individuals and I was just this very moment saying Solomon Northup is an expert player on

17
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:10,780
the violin. He was indeed. Mr. Moon is being overly gracious. Well, take it into consideration

18
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:15,240
his graciousness. Your modesty, may we trouble you for a moment of your time to converse, sir?

19
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:22,900
Of course. A circus. That is our usual employee. The company currently in the city of Washington.

20
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:27,240
Circus too constricting a word to describe the talented and merry band with which we travel.

21
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:32,460
It is a spectacle unlike most have ever witnessed. Creatures from the darkest Africa

22
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:35,760
get unseen by civilized men, acrobats from the Orient

23
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:39,340
who contort themselves in the most confounding manners.

24
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:40,960
And I myself, in aid of Mr. Brown,

25
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,140
an internationally renowned practitioner

26
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,680
in the art of prestidigitation.

27
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,680
We are on our way thither to rejoin the company,

28
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,900
having left for a short time to make a small profit

29
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:49,940
from our own exhibition.

30
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,860
The reason for our inquiry with Mr. Moon.

31
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,640
Yes, we had just a devil of a time

32
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:55,600
in procuring music for entertainments.

33
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,020
Men of true talents are seemingly in short supply.

34
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,240
Thank you, sir.

35
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,700
If we could persuade you to accompany us

36
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:05,480
us as far as Washington. We could give you one dollar for each day's services and three dollars

37
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:09,500
for every night played at our performances. In addition, we will provide sufficient pay for your

38
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:19,320
return here to Saratoga two weeks from today. Welcome to Washington, Solomon.

39
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:37,690
Today? Not too much. Some say not enough. Solomon, $43 all to you. That is far more than my wages

40
00:10:37,690 --> 00:10:50,740
a mountain. It's been a most profitable week. Cheers. Cheers. Cheers. Another. Gentlemen,

41
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:59,520
your generosity is extraordinary. And your talents are undeniable. To Solomon. Cheers.

42
00:11:00,200 --> 00:12:15,280
Cheers. It's all right, Solomon. There's no shame in it. No shame at all. Too many libations?

43
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,280
Halfway there.

44
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:37,690
We won't hear it. We won't.

45
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:39,690
Let him sleep, Hamilton.

46
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:42,690
A good night's rest.

47
00:12:42,690 --> 00:12:50,200
And tomorrow, tomorrow you will feel as well and refreshed as if the Earth were new again.

48
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:53,200
Hamilton, there's nothing more we can do for him.

49
00:12:53,200 --> 00:13:08,870
Well, boy, how you feel now?

50
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:15,300
My name, my name is Solomon Northam.

51
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:19,260
I'm a free man, a resident of Saratoga, New York,

52
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:22,060
the residence of my wife and children, who are equally free.

53
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,100
And you have no right whatsoever to detain me.

54
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:25,620
You're not any free man.

55
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:29,000
And I promise you, I promise you upon my liberation,

56
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:33,300
I will have satisfaction for this wrong.

57
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:35,180
Resolve this.

58
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:44,660
Produce your papers.

59
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:47,080
You're no free man.

60
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,520
And you ain't from Saratoga.

61
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:54,990
You're from Georgia.

62
00:13:54,990 --> 00:13:58,520
You ain't a free man.

63
00:13:58,520 --> 00:14:04,630
You're nothing but a Georgia runaway.

64
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:08,810
You're just a runaway nigger.

65
00:14:08,810 --> 00:16:35,960
You a slave?

66
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:38,280
Yours is just rags and tatters.

67
00:16:38,280 --> 00:17:24,090
You need something proper to wear.

68
00:17:24,090 --> 00:17:38,270
Rags and tatters, rags and tatters.

69
00:17:38,270 --> 00:17:42,690
Come on, wash up.

70
00:17:42,690 --> 00:17:47,120
The boy too, get him clean.

71
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:48,740
Scrub now.

72
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:51,440
You know my mama will come?

73
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,340
Then hush him up.

74
00:17:52,340 --> 00:17:56,530
Mama, mama.

75
00:17:56,530 --> 00:18:10,280
Hush him up.

76
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:13,460
We need a sympathetic ear, an opportunity

77
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,840
to explain our situation.

78
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:16,880
Who, in your estimation, is that sympathetic ear?

79
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,880
The two men I journeyed with.

80
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:20,960
I'm certain they're making inquiries at this very moment.

81
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:22,880
I'll be just as certain they're counting the money paid

82
00:18:22,880 --> 00:18:23,880
for delivering you to this place.

83
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:24,880
They were not kidnappers.

84
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:27,020
They were artists, fellow performers.

85
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,640
You know that?

86
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:32,370
You know for certain who they were?

87
00:18:32,370 --> 00:18:36,650
The reality to come is us being transported southward.

88
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:40,330
New Orleans, if I was to venture, after we arrive,

89
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:42,070
will be put to market.

90
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:46,110
And beyond that, well, I suppose once in a slave state,

91
00:18:46,110 --> 00:18:47,110
there's only one outcome.

92
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:48,010
No.

93
00:18:48,010 --> 00:18:49,990
I don't say that to give you empty agitation, John.

94
00:18:49,990 --> 00:18:52,030
For y'all, for y'all, there ain't nothing but the help

95
00:18:52,030 --> 00:18:53,530
of John Wilson kidnapped.

96
00:18:53,530 --> 00:18:56,150
John's just being held as dead, that's all.

97
00:18:56,150 --> 00:18:58,150
Master, please, let John be redeemed.

98
00:18:58,150 --> 00:18:59,730
Boy, our masters will not come for us.

99
00:18:59,730 --> 00:19:01,150
John, John, I'm sorry for y'all,

100
00:19:01,150 --> 00:19:02,530
but that's how it be where you're going.

101
00:19:02,530 --> 00:19:04,210
You're going without John.

102
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:21,120
Mama, Brad.

103
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:22,840
Come on, get up.

104
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:23,740
I said get up.

105
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:24,640
No, no, don't.

106
00:19:24,640 --> 00:19:26,020
Now, I don't want to hear you talk.

107
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:26,920
Get in the yard.

108
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:27,820
Not my children.

109
00:19:27,820 --> 00:19:29,320
Ain't no need for all that.

110
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,480
Just taking a little trip.

111
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,880
That's all.

112
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,860
Don't want to frighten the children over a little boat

113
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:35,400
ride, do you?

114
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:37,240
That master's going to pay his debt.

115
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:38,140
Line up.

116
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:45,410
This master's going to pay his debt.

117
00:19:45,410 --> 00:19:49,070
I don't want to hear a word out of none of you.

118
00:19:49,070 --> 00:20:03,840
Not a one.

119
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,370
Come on.

120
00:20:06,370 --> 00:20:07,270
Move.

121
00:20:07,270 --> 00:20:11,400
Come on.

122
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,960
Follow your mama.

123
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:13,860
Come on, boy.

124
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:14,760
Come on.

125
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:15,660
Up you step.

126
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:24,980
of that wagon. Come on. Come on, move it. Let's go, come on. Up the stairs. Come on, let's go.

127
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:38,900
Come on, move it. All right, come on. Hey, you, go on, get up. Sit down right there.

128
00:20:44,940 --> 00:21:38,050
Right there, sit down. Cheer and don't be so cast down. If you want to survive, do and say as little

129
00:21:38,050 --> 00:21:47,820
as possible tell no one who you really are and tell no one you can read and write unless you

130
00:21:47,820 --> 00:22:22,280
want to be a dead nigga your mouth shut we're well planned i believe they could be strong

131
00:22:22,280 --> 00:22:29,500
three can't go against the whole crew the rest here are niggas born and bred slaves

132
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:36,460
niggas ain't got no stomach for a fight not a damn one boss i know we get we were traveling

133
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:38,460
We wish we'd die trying.

134
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:40,460
Survival's not about certain death.

135
00:22:40,460 --> 00:22:43,460
It's about keeping your head down.

136
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:49,310
Days ago, I was with my family in my home,

137
00:22:49,310 --> 00:23:00,460
telling no one who I am.

138
00:23:00,460 --> 00:23:01,460
That's the way to survive.

139
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:06,950
Well, I don't want to survive.

140
00:23:06,950 --> 00:25:14,840
My solicitor has documentation verifying

141
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:17,840
the negro known as Clemens Ray is my property.

142
00:25:17,840 --> 00:25:19,840
I know nothing of this arrangement.

143
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:21,840
You are ordered to return that property immediately

144
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:23,840
or be charged with thievery.

145
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,840
Free him!

146
00:25:25,840 --> 00:26:47,940
Mr. Parker.

147
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:49,940
Ah, Mr. Northup.

148
00:26:49,940 --> 00:26:51,940
Mrs. Northup.

149
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:53,940
Solomon, could I interest you in a new cravat?

150
00:26:53,940 --> 00:26:55,940
Pure silk by way of the French.

151
00:26:55,940 --> 00:26:57,940
We're in need of a fresh carry-off.

152
00:26:57,940 --> 00:26:59,940
My missus is Travis. Nothing more.

153
00:26:59,940 --> 00:27:01,940
The year has passed already.

154
00:27:01,940 --> 00:27:03,940
Off to work at Sandy Hill again?

155
00:27:03,940 --> 00:27:05,940
I am. I have just the thing.

156
00:27:05,940 --> 00:27:07,940
Something to suit your style,

157
00:27:07,940 --> 00:27:09,940
and yet sturdy enough for the 40-mile round trip.

158
00:27:09,940 --> 00:27:11,940
It's beautiful. At what price?

159
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:13,940
We will take it.

160
00:27:13,940 --> 00:27:16,440
Come see what your father has just purchased for me.

161
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:18,440
One moment, sir, and you'll be assisted.

162
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:21,440
Mr. Parker, sir, if we could discuss the pricing.

163
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:22,940
Forgive me, Solomon.

164
00:27:22,940 --> 00:27:24,440
Mrs. Northup, a customer waits.

165
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:25,440
Welcome, sir.

166
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:27,440
Shop well, sir, but mind your wallet.

167
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:29,440
Pay no attention to this gentleman's nonsense.

168
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:30,440
Jesper!

169
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:34,040
My regrets for the intrusion, sir.

170
00:27:34,040 --> 00:27:35,540
No intrusion.

171
00:27:35,540 --> 00:27:41,100
Good day, sir.

172
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:42,600
Good day.

173
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,100
Jesper.

174
00:27:44,100 --> 00:27:55,580
Very good, very good.

175
00:27:55,580 --> 00:27:56,580
Let's see here.

176
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:57,580
Eliza!

177
00:27:57,580 --> 00:28:21,170
Stand up when you hear your name. Eliza, Leffy, John, Oren, Platt. Stand up.

178
00:28:21,170 --> 00:28:26,350
You fit the description given. Why didn't you answer when called?

179
00:28:26,350 --> 00:28:31,360
My name's not Platt. My name...

180
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:36,800
Your name is Platt. Captain, get these niggers to my cart.

181
00:28:36,800 --> 00:29:09,640
I believe I have something very much to your liking in the back room. Follow me, please.

182
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:12,640
Yes, now, inspect them at your leisure,

183
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:17,640
but I ask you to pay particular regard to young Ezra here.

184
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:19,640
Incredibly sound limbs.

185
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:21,640
I have never seen anything quite like him.

186
00:29:21,640 --> 00:29:23,640
And this marvelous creature. Can you believe it?

187
00:29:23,640 --> 00:29:25,640
Hmm? To make a fine lady's maid?

188
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:27,640
Yes, madam.

189
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:29,640
So, inspect at your leisure,

190
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:31,640
take your time, help yourself to refreshments.

191
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:34,640
Gentlemen, what catches your fancy here?

192
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:36,640
Hmm? This boy?

193
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:38,640
Yes, open your mouth. Open wider.

194
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:41,480
Look in there. Never been sick a day in his life.

195
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:43,480
And I call particular attention to Martha.

196
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:45,480
She is an excellent pastry cook.

197
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:47,480
Ah, Mr. Ford.

198
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,480
Splendid seeing you, sir.

199
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:52,480
What catches your fancy? This lad is very brawny.

200
00:29:52,480 --> 00:29:55,480
How much are the wands, Platt and Eliza?

201
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:57,480
Ah, yes.

202
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,480
1,000 for Platt.

203
00:29:59,480 --> 00:30:02,480
Oh, this is a nigger of considerable talent, I assure you.

204
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:04,480
700 for Eliza?

205
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:06,480
My fairest price?

206
00:30:06,480 --> 00:30:09,860
You would accept a note?

207
00:30:09,860 --> 00:30:11,860
Please, sir, do not divide my family.

208
00:30:11,860 --> 00:30:13,860
Do not take me unless you take my choice.

209
00:30:13,860 --> 00:30:15,860
Liza, quiet!

210
00:30:15,860 --> 00:30:17,860
You will have the most faithful slave in me,

211
00:30:17,860 --> 00:30:19,860
the most faithful slave that has ever lived,

212
00:30:19,860 --> 00:30:21,860
but I beg that you do not separate us.

213
00:30:21,860 --> 00:30:23,860
Stop it. I will give you something to cry about.

214
00:30:23,860 --> 00:30:25,860
Randall, come forward. Come, come, come.

215
00:30:25,860 --> 00:30:27,860
Now, you see how fit this boy is.

216
00:30:27,860 --> 00:30:29,860
You know, like ripe fruit.

217
00:30:29,860 --> 00:30:31,860
May I take your stick a moment?

218
00:30:31,860 --> 00:30:33,860
Observe this, Randall.

219
00:30:33,860 --> 00:30:35,860
Jump, jump, jump, run, run, run.

220
00:30:35,860 --> 00:30:37,860
Good. Higher.

221
00:30:37,860 --> 00:30:42,360
Do you see this? Very likely, he will grow into a fine beast.

222
00:30:42,360 --> 00:30:45,860
Ah, 600 for the boy.

223
00:30:45,860 --> 00:30:47,860
Fair and final.

224
00:30:47,860 --> 00:30:49,360
Done.

225
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:51,860
Superb. A moment, please.

226
00:30:51,860 --> 00:30:53,860
Mr. Ford.

227
00:30:53,860 --> 00:30:54,860
Eliza!

228
00:30:54,860 --> 00:30:56,860
How much for the little girl?

229
00:30:56,860 --> 00:31:01,300
No use for her. One so young will bring you no profit.

230
00:31:01,300 --> 00:31:03,300
No, no, no, no. I cannot sell the girl.

231
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:06,800
There's heaps and piles of money to be made from her.

232
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:09,300
She's a beauty, one of the regular bloods.

233
00:31:09,300 --> 00:31:12,300
Well, none of you thick-lipped, bullet-headed, cotton-picking niggers here.

234
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:14,300
A child, man.

235
00:31:14,300 --> 00:31:18,120
For God's sake, you're not sentimental in the least.

236
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:22,120
Ah, my sentimentality extends the length of a coin.

237
00:31:23,120 --> 00:31:25,120
Now, do you take this lot?

238
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:30,680
Mr. Fordo, do you pass on them all?

239
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,680
I will take the ones Platt and Eliza sold.

240
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:34,680
Eliza and Platt. Splendid.

241
00:31:38,280 --> 00:31:39,280
Get her out of here!

242
00:31:39,280 --> 00:31:50,150
Are they keeping something to cry about, you goddamn wimps?

243
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:52,510
Get the hell out of here, kid! Out now! Out!

244
00:32:01,110 --> 00:32:01,510
Pleasure.

245
00:32:01,890 --> 00:32:19,730
Bring all those niggers.

246
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:21,430
Two of them.

247
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:23,030
You got two.

248
00:32:23,550 --> 00:32:24,330
Mr. Chapin.

249
00:32:25,390 --> 00:32:26,230
This one's crying.

250
00:32:27,110 --> 00:32:28,170
Why is this one crying?

251
00:32:28,390 --> 00:32:29,450
Separated from her children.

252
00:32:29,550 --> 00:32:30,290
Oh, dear.

253
00:32:30,510 --> 00:32:31,230
Couldn't be helped.

254
00:32:31,710 --> 00:32:32,630
Poor, poor woman.

255
00:32:32,950 --> 00:32:33,630
Mr. Chapin.

256
00:32:33,810 --> 00:32:34,170
Yes, sir.

257
00:32:34,430 --> 00:32:36,970
Tomorrow you can take these two up to the mill, start them working.

258
00:32:37,590 --> 00:32:40,730
For now, make them adequate, fix them a meal, and have them rest themselves.

259
00:32:41,010 --> 00:32:41,510
Yes, sir.

260
00:32:42,830 --> 00:32:43,610
Come on, now.

261
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:45,670
Come on. Don't dawdle.

262
00:32:45,670 --> 00:32:48,670
Something to eat and some rest.

263
00:32:48,670 --> 00:32:50,670
Your children will soon be forgotten.

264
00:32:50,670 --> 00:33:20,130
Now, for all of you raw niggers that don't know,

265
00:33:20,130 --> 00:33:22,130
my name is John Tibbets,

266
00:33:22,130 --> 00:33:25,130
William Ford's chief carpenter.

267
00:33:25,130 --> 00:33:28,130
You will refer to me as Master.

268
00:33:28,130 --> 00:33:32,130
Now, Mr. Chapin is the overseer on this plantation.

269
00:33:32,130 --> 00:33:36,130
You, too, will refer to him as Master.

270
00:33:36,130 --> 00:33:39,380
So clap your hands.

271
00:33:39,380 --> 00:33:58,790
hands like this come on come on clap your hands nigga run nigga flow nigga tall his shirt in two

272
00:33:58,790 --> 00:34:09,590
run run the patty roll look at you run nigga run well you better get away that's right like you

273
00:34:09,590 --> 00:34:18,390
mean it nigga run run so fast over his head and on his nest run run the patty roll look at you

274
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:20,510
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

275
00:34:20,510 --> 00:34:24,190
Run, nigga, run, the patty roller gets you

276
00:34:24,190 --> 00:34:26,470
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

277
00:34:26,470 --> 00:34:30,690
Some folks say a nigga don't steal

278
00:34:30,690 --> 00:34:32,810
I caught three in my cornfield

279
00:34:32,810 --> 00:34:35,150
One has a bushel and one has a pack

280
00:34:35,150 --> 00:34:37,550
One has a rope, it was hung around his neck

281
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:40,330
Run, nigga, run, the patty roller gets you

282
00:34:40,330 --> 00:34:42,350
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

283
00:34:42,350 --> 00:34:45,050
Run, nigga, run, the patty roller gets you

284
00:34:45,050 --> 00:34:47,210
Run, nigga, run, well, you better get away

285
00:34:47,850 --> 00:34:50,470
Hey, Mr. Patti-Roller, don't catch me.

286
00:34:50,510 --> 00:34:52,790
Catch that nigga behind that tree!

287
00:34:52,850 --> 00:34:53,890
Run, nigga, run.

288
00:34:53,950 --> 00:34:55,390
The Patti-Roller'll catch you.

289
00:34:55,450 --> 00:34:56,310
Run, nigga, run.

290
00:34:57,550 --> 00:34:58,550
Run, nigga, run.

291
00:34:58,850 --> 00:34:59,950
The Patti-Roller'll catch you.

292
00:34:59,990 --> 00:35:00,890
Run, nigga, run.

293
00:35:00,950 --> 00:35:02,230
Where you better get away.

294
00:35:02,250 --> 00:35:03,450
Run, nigga, run.

295
00:35:03,530 --> 00:35:04,790
The Patti-Roller'll catch you.

296
00:35:04,830 --> 00:35:05,730
Run, nigga, run.

297
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:06,890
Where you better get away.

298
00:35:06,970 --> 00:35:10,230
I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac,

299
00:35:10,290 --> 00:35:11,570
and the God of Jacob.

300
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:15,410
When the multitude heard this,

301
00:35:15,470 --> 00:35:17,210
they were astonished at his doctors,

302
00:35:17,210 --> 00:35:21,210
And then one of them, which was a lawyer,

303
00:35:21,210 --> 00:35:24,210
asked him a question, tempting him.

304
00:35:29,210 --> 00:36:23,860
The creek is plenty deep enough to sail,

305
00:36:23,860 --> 00:36:25,860
even with a boat full of load.

306
00:36:25,860 --> 00:36:28,860
The distance from the work area to the point on the Ladder Bayou

307
00:36:28,860 --> 00:36:30,860
is several miles by water fewer than land.

308
00:36:30,860 --> 00:36:32,860
It occurs to me that the expense of transportation

309
00:36:32,860 --> 00:36:33,860
would be materially diminished...

310
00:36:33,860 --> 00:36:34,860
Materially diminished?

311
00:36:34,860 --> 00:36:36,860
...if we used the waterway.

312
00:36:36,860 --> 00:36:39,620
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

313
00:36:39,620 --> 00:36:44,130
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

314
00:36:44,130 --> 00:36:47,330
Let the man say his piece.

315
00:36:47,330 --> 00:36:50,910
It's a scheme plenty of engineers have schemed similarly.

316
00:36:50,910 --> 00:36:53,830
The passes are too tight.

317
00:36:53,830 --> 00:36:57,050
I reckon they're more than 12 feet at their most narrow.

318
00:36:57,050 --> 00:36:58,510
Wide enough for a tub to traverse

319
00:36:58,510 --> 00:37:00,310
if a team of niggers cleared it out.

320
00:37:00,310 --> 00:37:03,170
And you know what of transport and terraforming?

321
00:37:03,170 --> 00:37:05,010
I labored repairing the Champlain Canal

322
00:37:05,010 --> 00:37:06,890
on the section over which William Van Nortwyk

323
00:37:06,890 --> 00:37:08,510
was superintendent.

324
00:37:08,510 --> 00:37:10,970
With my earnings, I hired several efficient engineers

325
00:37:10,970 --> 00:37:15,430
hands to assist me and ended into contracts for the transportation of large rafts of timber from

326
00:37:15,430 --> 00:37:25,340
lake champlain to troy well i'll admit to being impressed even if you won't collect the team and

327
00:37:25,340 --> 00:37:36,000
see what good you can do all right

328
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Let's clear it up.

329
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:50,750
One, two, three, four.

330
00:37:50,750 --> 00:37:52,750
Hey, boy.

331
00:37:52,750 --> 00:37:53,750
I'm fat.

332
00:37:53,750 --> 00:37:58,270
I'm strong.

333
00:37:58,270 --> 00:37:59,270
Yes.

334
00:37:59,270 --> 00:38:01,580
I'm tall.

335
00:38:01,580 --> 00:38:03,580
Yes, sir.

336
00:38:03,580 --> 00:38:11,280
Flat, you are a marvel.

337
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:21,310
What took you so long?

338
00:38:21,310 --> 00:38:23,310
Thank you, Master Voight.

339
00:38:23,310 --> 00:38:24,310
Oh, thank you.

340
00:38:24,310 --> 00:38:25,310
Yeah.

341
00:38:25,310 --> 00:38:26,310
All right, marvel.

342
00:38:26,310 --> 00:38:27,310
Yes, sir.

343
00:38:27,310 --> 00:38:28,310
Yeah, sir.

344
00:38:28,310 --> 00:38:29,310
All right, we're good.

345
00:38:29,310 --> 00:38:30,310
All right.

346
00:38:30,310 --> 00:38:31,310
Yeah.

347
00:38:31,310 --> 00:38:32,310
Whoo!

348
00:38:32,310 --> 00:38:33,310
I'll beat that.

349
00:38:33,310 --> 00:38:34,310
I'll beat that.

350
00:38:34,310 --> 00:38:36,530
Oh, that's a pleasant ending, yeah.

351
00:38:40,400 --> 00:38:42,280
Oh, plaid.

352
00:38:42,660 --> 00:39:04,040
My great thanks, Master Ford.

353
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:05,880
My thanks to you.

354
00:39:06,980 --> 00:39:08,080
It is the least of it.

355
00:39:09,460 --> 00:39:12,040
I hope it brings us both much joy over the years.

356
00:39:40,750 --> 00:40:00,230
Stop your wailing.

357
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:06,340
You let yourself be overcome by sorrow, you will drown in it.

358
00:40:06,860 --> 00:40:08,440
Have you stopped crying for your children?

359
00:40:08,980 --> 00:40:13,600
You make no sounds, but will you ever let them go in your heart?

360
00:40:18,640 --> 00:40:20,000
That's my flesh.

361
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,160
Then who is distressed?

362
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:24,600
Do I upset the master and the mistress?

363
00:40:25,340 --> 00:40:27,980
Do you care less about my loss than their well-being?

364
00:40:28,020 --> 00:40:29,320
Master Ford is a decent man.

365
00:40:29,340 --> 00:40:30,400
He is a slaver.

366
00:40:30,580 --> 00:40:31,560
Under the circumstances.

367
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:33,460
Under the circumstances, he's a slaver.

368
00:40:33,860 --> 00:40:35,240
Will you truckle at his boot?

369
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:35,520
No.

370
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:37,360
You luxuriate in his favor.

371
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:37,940
I survive.

372
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:41,060
I will not fall into despair.

373
00:40:41,620 --> 00:40:43,580
I will offer up my talents to Master Ford.

374
00:40:43,740 --> 00:40:46,500
I will keep myself hearty till freedom is opportune.

375
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:48,040
Oh, Ford, is your opportunity?

376
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:52,040
You think he does not know that you are more than you suggest.

377
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:55,040
But he does nothing for you. Nothing.

378
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:59,040
You are no better than prized livestock.

379
00:40:59,040 --> 00:41:01,040
Call for him. Call.

380
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:03,040
Tell him of your previous circumstances

381
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:05,040
and see what it earns you, Solomon.

382
00:41:05,040 --> 00:41:09,990
So you settle into your role as Platt, then?

383
00:41:09,990 --> 00:41:14,720
My back is thick with scars

384
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:16,720
for protesting my freedom.

385
00:41:16,720 --> 00:41:23,630
I accuse you of nothing I cannot accuse.

386
00:41:23,630 --> 00:41:32,650
I have done dishonorable things to survive and for all of them I have been no better than if I had stood up for myself.

387
00:41:32,650 --> 00:41:39,260
Solomon, let me weep for my children.

388
00:41:49,610 --> 00:41:57,610
Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.

389
00:41:58,610 --> 00:42:03,610
And whoso shall receive one such little child in my name, receiveth me.

390
00:42:03,610 --> 00:42:05,610
I cannot have that kind of depression about.

391
00:42:05,610 --> 00:42:17,140
But whoso shall offend one of these little ones, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck and he were drowned in the depth of the sea.

392
00:42:17,140 --> 00:42:18,140
Amen.

393
00:42:32,690 --> 00:42:34,690
Make them boards flush.

394
00:42:34,690 --> 00:42:35,690
They are, sir.

395
00:42:35,690 --> 00:42:37,690
Now, they is no such thing.

396
00:42:37,690 --> 00:42:42,510
They are smooth to the touch as a yearling's coat.

397
00:42:42,510 --> 00:42:47,140
Are you calling me a liar, boy?

398
00:42:47,140 --> 00:42:52,790
That's all a matter of perspective, sir.

399
00:42:52,790 --> 00:42:56,790
From where you stand you may see differently, but the hands are not mistaken.

400
00:42:56,790 --> 00:43:00,790
Simply ask that you use all your senses before rendering judgment.

401
00:43:00,790 --> 00:43:08,930
Oh, my, you are a brute. You are a dog.

402
00:43:08,930 --> 00:43:11,930
And no better for following instruction!

403
00:43:11,930 --> 00:43:14,750
I'll do as ordered.

404
00:43:14,750 --> 00:43:16,750
Well, then you'll be up at daybreak.

405
00:43:16,750 --> 00:43:20,750
You'll procure a keg of nails from Chapin and commence to putting on clabberts.

406
00:43:20,750 --> 00:43:21,750
Yes, sir.

407
00:43:21,750 --> 00:43:29,610
Make them boards flush.

408
00:43:29,610 --> 00:44:04,700
When I say I have my master's favor, you understand.

409
00:44:04,700 --> 00:44:12,460
And for nine years he blessed me with every comfort and luxury in life,

410
00:44:12,460 --> 00:44:17,460
silks and jewels and even servants to wait upon us.

411
00:44:19,460 --> 00:44:22,460
And such was our life.

412
00:44:22,460 --> 00:44:25,460
And the life of this beautiful girl I bore for him,

413
00:44:25,460 --> 00:44:31,940
my Master Barry's daughter,

414
00:44:31,940 --> 00:44:34,940
she always looked at me with an unkind nature.

415
00:44:34,940 --> 00:44:38,940
And she hated Emily, no matter she and Emily were flesh or flesh.

416
00:44:38,940 --> 00:44:45,050
As Master Barry's health failed, she gained power in the household,

417
00:44:45,050 --> 00:44:49,050
and eventually I was brought to the city under the false pretense

418
00:44:49,050 --> 00:44:51,050
of our free papers being executed.

419
00:44:51,050 --> 00:44:52,050
Poor children.

420
00:44:52,050 --> 00:45:39,400
I thought I told you to commence to putting on clapboards.

421
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:43,400
Yes, Master, I'm about it. These have all been replaced.

422
00:45:44,400 --> 00:45:46,400
Well, didn't I tell you to get a keg of nails?

423
00:45:47,400 --> 00:45:48,400
And so I did.

424
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:55,210
Goddamn you, I thought you knowed something!

425
00:45:55,210 --> 00:45:56,210
I did as instructed.

426
00:45:56,210 --> 00:45:59,210
If there's something wrong, it's wrong with the instruction.

427
00:45:59,210 --> 00:46:01,900
with the instruction.

428
00:46:01,900 --> 00:46:05,580
Bastard.

429
00:46:05,580 --> 00:46:08,820
Goddamn black bastard.

430
00:46:08,820 --> 00:46:13,220
Strip your clothes.

431
00:46:13,220 --> 00:46:14,060
Strip.

432
00:46:14,060 --> 00:46:52,980
Another day, nigga.

433
00:46:52,980 --> 00:46:55,140
What is the matter?

434
00:46:55,140 --> 00:46:56,860
Master Tibbies wants to whoop me for using

435
00:46:56,860 --> 00:47:02,520
the nails you gave me.

436
00:47:02,520 --> 00:47:04,920
I will have.

437
00:47:04,920 --> 00:47:10,980
And I will have all of it.

438
00:47:10,980 --> 00:47:13,740
Master, do not leave the plantation,

439
00:47:13,740 --> 00:47:16,460
for if you run, I cannot protect you.

440
00:47:16,460 --> 00:48:22,500
Stay here.

441
00:48:22,500 --> 00:48:24,600
Whoever moves that nigger's a dead man.

442
00:48:25,980 --> 00:48:29,260
I am the overseer on this plantation.

443
00:48:30,020 --> 00:48:32,400
William Ford holds the mortgage on Platt.

444
00:48:32,920 --> 00:48:35,620
If you bang him, he will lose his debt.

445
00:48:35,960 --> 00:48:37,880
You have no claim to his life.

446
00:48:38,600 --> 00:48:43,080
As for you two, if you have any regard for your own safety,

447
00:48:43,840 --> 00:48:44,780
I say be gone!

448
00:48:48,410 --> 00:48:49,950
You got no cause!

449
00:48:50,410 --> 00:48:53,710
The plot is mine, and mine to do with as I please!

450
00:48:53,950 --> 00:48:54,670
You touch!

451
00:49:10,630 --> 00:49:25,820
Get Master Ford!

452
00:49:25,820 --> 00:53:04,020
Long as they fear him, I don't believe you will remain passive at Tibby to tax.

453
00:53:05,080 --> 00:53:07,640
I have transferred my debt to Edwin Epps.

454
00:53:08,380 --> 00:53:09,560
He will take charge.

455
00:53:09,880 --> 00:53:39,470
I cannot hear that.

456
00:53:39,510 --> 00:53:41,710
Before I came to you, I was a free man.

457
00:53:41,810 --> 00:53:43,190
Trying to save your life.

458
00:53:45,580 --> 00:53:48,160
And I have a debt to be mindful of.

459
00:53:50,600 --> 00:53:52,280
And that is to Edwin Epps now.

460
00:53:52,820 --> 00:53:55,620
He is a hard man, prides himself on being a nigger breaker,

461
00:53:55,620 --> 00:53:58,000
but truthfully, I could find no others who would take him.

462
00:53:59,220 --> 00:54:00,840
You've made a reputation of yourself.

463
00:54:00,940 --> 00:54:05,940
Whatever the circumstances, you are an exceptional nigger, Platt.

464
00:54:05,940 --> 00:54:10,890
But I fear no good will come of it.

465
00:54:10,890 --> 00:54:39,270
And that servant which knew his lord's will,

466
00:54:39,270 --> 00:54:43,680
which knew his lord's will,

467
00:54:43,680 --> 00:54:55,080
and prepared not himself, prepared not himself,

468
00:54:55,080 --> 00:55:02,210
neither did according to his will,

469
00:55:02,210 --> 00:55:08,350
shall be beaten with many stripes.

470
00:55:08,350 --> 00:55:10,350
Did you hear that?

471
00:55:10,350 --> 00:55:12,350
Stripes.

472
00:55:12,350 --> 00:55:15,350
That nigger that don't obey his lord,

473
00:55:15,350 --> 00:55:18,350
that's his master, d'you see?

474
00:55:18,350 --> 00:55:23,350
That there nigger shall be beaten with many stripes.

475
00:55:23,350 --> 00:55:28,790
Now, many signifies a great many.

476
00:55:28,790 --> 00:55:32,790
40, 100, 150 lashes.

477
00:55:32,790 --> 00:55:39,430
That's scripture.

478
00:55:39,430 --> 00:56:26,470
What you got for James 295 pounds it's real good boy it's real good 182 for Platt

479
00:56:26,470 --> 00:56:30,310
How much can even an average nigga pick a day?

480
00:56:31,310 --> 00:56:32,110
200 pounds.

481
00:56:32,830 --> 00:56:33,890
This nigga ain't even average.

482
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:38,620
512 pounds for Patsy.

483
00:56:40,140 --> 00:56:40,620
512!

484
00:56:42,220 --> 00:56:45,800
Your menfolk got no shame letting Patsy out pick you.

485
00:56:48,220 --> 00:56:50,760
Day ain't yet come, she swung lower than 500 pounds.

486
00:56:55,260 --> 00:56:56,560
You feel she is.

487
00:56:58,280 --> 00:56:59,120
138 pounds.

488
00:56:59,140 --> 00:56:59,760
I ain't done, Treech.

489
00:56:59,760 --> 00:57:03,940
Ain't I owed a minute to luxuriate on the work Patsy done?

490
00:57:05,140 --> 00:57:05,980
Yes, sir.

491
00:57:29,020 --> 00:57:30,980
The lesson and the rewards of righteous living.

492
00:57:33,880 --> 00:57:37,640
All be observant to that. All.

493
00:57:43,980 --> 00:57:45,360
138 pounds for Phoebe.

494
00:57:46,700 --> 00:57:49,100
Hit 145 yesterday. Pull her out.

495
00:57:51,340 --> 00:57:52,900
206 pounds for George.

496
00:57:53,220 --> 00:57:54,260
How much you pick yesterday?

497
00:57:56,440 --> 00:57:57,000
229.

498
00:57:58,960 --> 00:58:02,890
Come on, kid. Come on.

499
00:58:03,770 --> 00:59:57,480
Come on boy move

500
00:59:58,040 --> 01:00:35,690
We'll sell the niggas

501
01:00:36,350 --> 01:00:38,210
sell little pants

502
01:00:38,210 --> 01:00:42,850
She picked with more vigor than any other nigga choose another to go no other

503
01:00:44,190 --> 01:01:24,540
Sell her or I'll take myself cuz I will read myself if you will before I do away with her. What you looking at?

504
01:01:24,540 --> 01:01:30,660
I won't spoil it.

505
01:01:30,660 --> 01:01:34,520
I will not.

506
01:01:34,520 --> 01:01:35,520
Dance.

507
01:01:35,520 --> 01:02:23,150
Dance is here.

508
01:02:23,150 --> 01:02:26,040
Platt.

509
01:02:26,040 --> 01:02:27,040
Yes, Mistress.

510
01:02:27,040 --> 01:02:32,150
Can you find your way to Bartholomew's?

511
01:02:32,150 --> 01:02:34,150
I can't, ma'am.

512
01:02:34,150 --> 01:02:36,150
This is a list of goods and sundries.

513
01:02:36,150 --> 01:02:39,150
You will take it to be filled and return immediately.

514
01:02:39,150 --> 01:02:41,150
Take your tag.

515
01:02:41,150 --> 01:02:43,150
Tell Bartholomew to add it to our debt.

516
01:02:43,150 --> 01:02:44,150
Yes, Mistress.

517
01:02:44,150 --> 01:02:48,170
Where you from, Platt?

518
01:02:48,170 --> 01:02:53,910
Tell me again.

519
01:02:53,910 --> 01:02:55,910
Washington.

520
01:02:55,910 --> 01:02:56,910
Who were you, Master?

521
01:02:56,910 --> 01:02:57,910
Master Namor Freeman.

522
01:02:57,910 --> 01:02:59,910
Was he a learned man?

523
01:02:59,910 --> 01:03:01,910
